  "result": "Perfect! All 188 tests pass. The payments feature is complete:\n\n**Created src/payments.js:**\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`: Records a payment on issued or partially_paid invoices\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Ensures invoice is issued or partially_paid (NOT_ISSUED)\n  - Checks that payment doesn't exceed remaining balance (OVERPAYMENT)\n  - Adds payment to payments array and updates status\n  - Status becomes 'paid' when balance is 0, otherwise 'partially_paid'\n  - Returns new invoice object (no mutation)\n\n- `balanceDue(invoice)`: Returns remaining amount owed (total - payments, clamped at 0)\n\n- `totalPaid(invoice)`: Returns sum of all recorded payments\n\n**Updated src/errors.js:**\n- Added NOT_ISSUED: \"Can only record payments on issued or partially paid invoices.\"\n- Added OVERPAYMENT: \"Payment exceeds the amount still owed.\"\n\n**Created test/payments.test.js with 17 tests covering:**\n- Balance calculations\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Multiple sequential payments\n- Error conditions: draft invoices, already paid invoices, non-integer amounts, zero/negative amounts, overpayments\n- Immutability verification\n- totalPaid summation",
